Subject: [PATCH 051/154] feat: the settings window, and Cmd+comma to open it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ONE PER PROCESS, not one per browser window. That is what Cmd+comma means on
this platform - it brings the settings window forward rather than opening
another - so this does not follow CommandBarWidget's shape, which is parented
to a browser window, covers it, and dies with it.

The chord is claimed in prePerformKeyEquivalent, on the raw NSEvent. A probe
measured why: on an HTML surface it reaches prePerform and never postPerform,
so the IDC intercept never sees it and un-gating that alone would have brought
nothing back. IsSettingsKeyEquivalent already existed, feeding only a
diagnostic probe; it has a caller now.

The window and its implementation are portable - no AppKit type in either -
so the Aura port inherits it. Only the chord that opens it is Mac-specific.

atrium.html was missing the stylesheet link, which the first run showed as an
unstyled row of buttons. Caught by looking at the capture, not by the
assertions, which were all green either way.

Verified by settings-cmd-comma, 4 of 4: the chord claimed, the window built,
settingsReady received, and TWO AXStandardWindows - the second titled 'Atrium
Settings' at 860x652. The three log lines land 34ms and 57ms after the chord,
which is the order that says one caused the next.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
